; Test: Mixing BTM (main space) and ACT (external file)
; ======================================================
;
; Prerequisites: Create ACT file first
;   ./examples/misc/make_fruit_colors_act.sh
;
; Pattern: (I (BTM <pat1>) (ACT file <pat2>))
; Combines queries from main space AND external ACT file!

; Setup: Preferences in main space
(likes Alice apple)
(likes Bob banana)
(likes Carol grape)

; Test: Find what color each person's favorite fruit is
; 1. (BTM (likes $person $fruit)) queries main space
; 2. (ACT fruit_colors (color $fruit $c)) queries ACT file
; 3. Both must agree on $fruit binding!

(exec 0
  (I (BTM (likes $person $fruit))
     (ACT fruit_colors (color $fruit $c)))
  (O (+ (preference $person likes $fruit which-is $c))))

; Expected:
; (preference Alice likes apple which-is red)
; (preference Bob likes banana which-is yellow)
; (preference Carol likes grape which-is purple)
;
; Key insight: Mix internal facts (BTM) with external data (ACT)!
; This is like a JOIN in databases.
